# This addon is a test fixture, not a shipped distribution, so its build output
# and its npm tree are generated rather than committed. In a real consumer addon
# `templates/*.pt` IS committed -- that is the whole point of the two-stage
# architecture -- and only `emails/node_modules` and `emails/.kit` are ignored.
src/emailkitdemo/templates/
src/emailkitdemo/emails/node_modules/
src/emailkitdemo/emails/package-lock.json
src/emailkitdemo/emails/.maizzle/
src/emailkitdemo/emails/.kit/
*.egg-info/
